---
description: Keep feature modules separated into focused, maintainable files
alwaysApply: true
---

# Module boundaries

- When code forms a distinct module or responsibility, place it in its own file instead of adding it to an unrelated large file.
- Keep application bootstrap files limited to composition, lifecycle wiring, and top-level orchestration.
- Separate procedural models, render passes, GLSL shader sources, controllers, math utilities, and UI behavior by responsibility.
- Put all procedural geometry generation under `src/models/` and import it through TypeScript modules.
- Prefer a focused directory with an `index.ts` public entry point when a subsystem contains multiple internal files.
- Avoid files that mix geometry generation, input handling, rendering setup, and shader source code.
- When adding a feature, extend the matching module or create a new focused module before editing the application entry point.

Example structure:

```text
src/
  controllers/FlyController.ts
  core/Renderer.ts
  math/mat4.ts
  models/terrain.ts
  models/grass.ts
  shaders/terrain.ts
  shaders/grass.ts
```
